    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0617" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1626a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-22T23:00:00-04:00">July 22, 1943—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4410. Deep concern was expressed by T. V. Soong regarding statement made at
                    Chungking by Chinese Minister of Communications regarding the new route for
                    supplies. A cable was sent by him to the Generalissimo<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d525-f1"/> immediately, to request that strict instructions be
                    issued to all officials that silence should be maintained regarding this
                    subject. (From Stettinius for Harriman.) The route is not as yet in operation.
                    (This is for your information.)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d525-f1" n="33" xml:id="d525-f1-content">
                <p>Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
